// Portable half of the #1367 SEAM 3 verification: the port-heap string BRIDGE
// that both platform transcripts rest on.
//
// `../rootiolinux` and `../rootiodarwin` check that a provider puts the right
// bytes on the right file descriptor. Both hand that provider a byte ADDRESS and
// a LENGTH, and both get them from `props`' `bytesOf`/`sizeOf`. If those were
// wrong, both transcripts would be wrong too — for a reason that has nothing to
// do with the code under test. This program checks them on their own, on EVERY
// target, so a failure names the layer that broke.
//
// It is also what makes `../rootio` a legal home for a shared props module: the
// stress harness enumerates every top-level directory under _tests_/stress and
// requires each one to be a runnable program with a golden, so a directory
// holding nothing but shared code fails the suite. Same arrangement as
// `../alloc` hosting `../alloc/props`.

import { bridgeProps, bridgeTotal } from "./props"

fn main() {
  print("rootio bridge=${bridgeProps()}/${bridgeTotal()}\n")
}
